Template: update-node-alternatives/default-version
Type: select
Choices: latest LTS, latest, none, custom
Default: none
_Description: Default Node.js version to install:
 update-node-alternatives can download a Node.js version through the
 bundled nvm and register it as the system-wide alternative right after
 the package is configured.
 .
  - "latest LTS" installs the most recent Long-Term Support release;
  - "latest" installs the most recent Node.js release;
  - "none" leaves the system without a Node.js version (the default);
  - "custom" lets you type a specific version string (e.g. v22.14.0,
    lts/jod, 20).
 .
 Choosing "none" is always safe: you can install or change the active
 version later with `update-node-alternatives --install <version>`.

Template: update-node-alternatives/custom-version
Type: string
_Description: Custom Node.js version to install:
 Type the Node.js version string to install. Anything accepted by
 `update-node-alternatives --install` (and ultimately by nvm) works:
 a major number (22), a full version (v22.14.0), or an alias
 (lts/jod, lts/*, node).

Template: update-node-alternatives/purge-nvm-store
Type: boolean
Default: false
_Description: Remove all installed Node.js versions on apt purge?
 update-node-alternatives stores Node.js versions under
 /usr/local/share/nvm/, outside dpkg's tree. By default `apt purge`
 leaves that store untouched.
 .
 When enabled, `apt purge` will also delete /usr/local/share/nvm/,
 along with every Node.js version installed through this package.
 The choice is recorded now and re-confirmed at purge time.
